"0" patch_number="2" project="chromiumos/chromite" project_url="https://chromium-review.googlesource.com/chromiumos/chromite" ref="refs/changes/08/448808/2" remote="cros" total_fail_count="0"/><pending_commit branch="master" change_id="I7a8b9a3eebe64c827e420646d30eda34e4f307aa" commit="b8f5d99b980dfe19d7939f9374c419302a8b28ec" commit_message="[sysmon] Move network metrics to its own module  BUG=chromium:698056 TEST=None  Change-Id: I7a8b9a3eebe64c827e420646d30eda34e4f307aa Reviewed-on: https://chromium-review.googlesource.com/448809 Commit-Ready: Allen Li &lt;ayatane@chromium.org&gt; Tested-by: Allen Li &lt;ayatane@chromium.org&gt; Reviewed-by: Allen Li &lt;ayatane@chromium.org&gt; " fail_count="0" gerrit_number="448809" owner_email="ayatane@chromium.org" pass_count="0" patch_number="2" project="chromiumos/chromite" project_url="https://chromium-review.googlesource.com/chromiumos/chromite" ref="refs/changes/09/448809/2" remote="cros" total_fail_count="0"/><pending_commit branch="chromeos-3.18" change_id="I7409be8d5cb2a2d66ebc16df568a271bbb9a1204" commit="b7cc779ef6f44c5e31c448f500d73dbb14ca6f04" commit_message="CHROMIUM: thermal: mediatek: skip svs late_init by default  Previously, we would always do mtk_svs_late_init, even if mtk_thermal itself didn't probe (ie, there was no &quot;mediatek,mt8173-thermal&quot; .dts node). In such a case, mtk_svs_late_init() would check the global skip_svs_init, which was false by default, and therefore proceed.  Eventually the system would crash because mtk thermal / SVS had not been probed.  This patch changes the global to allow_svs_late_init so we can still keep it in .bss (eg default false), but have it protect us from this potential situation.  Fixes: 5be71f4c13d3 (&quot;BACKPORT: FROMLIST: PM / AVS: thermal: MT8173:  Introduce support for SVS engine&quot;)  Signed-off-by: Daniel Kurtz &lt;djkurtz@chromium.org&gt;  BUG=chrome-os-partner:60805 TEST=Remove thermal node from mt8173.dtsi, build and boot to UI.  =&gt; No system crash at boot  Change-Id: I7409be8d5cb2a2d66ebc16df568a271bbb9a1204 Reviewed-on: https://chromium-review.googlesource.com/448776 Commit-Ready: Daniel Kurtz &lt;djkurtz@chromium.org&gt; Tested-by: Yidi Lin &lt;yidi.lin@mediatek.com&gt; Reviewed-by: Yidi Lin &lt;yidi.lin@mediatek.com&gt; Reviewed-by: Nicolas Boichat &lt;drinkcat@chromium.org&gt; " fail_count="0" gerrit_number="448776" owner_email="djkurtz@chromium.org" pass_count="0" patch_number="1" project="chromiumos/third_party/kernel" project_url="https://chromium-review.googlesource.com/chromiumos/third_party/kernel" ref="refs/changes/76/448776/1" remote="cros" total_fail_count="0"/><pending_commit branch="chromeos-3.18" change_id="Ic80916c5d054c1db3a0cbd502286f9ccb410f2be" commit="0ae9406cef8b1aa5175ef98241e7069b127feeae" commit_message="CHROMIUM: thermal: mediatek: SVS: remove pm_qos if cpufreq_get_policy fails  We add a pm_qos before looping over SVS banks.  Therefore, we must clean up in every error path.  If we don't, there may be a difficult to debug crash later when some other driver tries to add/modify/remove a pm_qos request.  Fixes: 5be71f4c13d3 (&quot;BACKPORT: FROMLIST: PM / AVS: thermal: MT8173:      Introduce support for SVS engine&quot;)  Signed-off-by: Daniel Kurtz &lt;djkurtz@chromium.org&gt; Signed-off-by: Yidi Lin &lt;yidi.lin@mediatek.com&gt;  BUG=b:35647992 TEST=Boot rowan to UI, test audio  =&gt; No kernel crash due to plist_add  Change-Id: Ic80916c5d054c1db3a0cbd502286f9ccb410f2be Reviewed-on: https://chromium-review.googlesource.com/448777 Commit-Ready: Daniel Kurtz &lt;djkurtz@chromium.org&gt; Tested-by: Yidi Lin &lt;yidi.lin@mediatek.com&gt; Reviewed-by: Yidi Lin &lt;yidi.lin@mediatek.com&gt; Reviewed-by: Nicolas Boichat &lt;drinkcat@chromium.org&gt; " fail_count="0" gerrit_number="448777" owner_email="djkurtz@chromium.org" pass_count="0" patch_number="1" project="chromiumos/third_party/kernel" project_url="https://chromium-review.googlesource.com/chromiumos/third_party/kernel" ref="refs/c